ing 冠心病 (coronary heart disease) and 食管静脉曲张破裂出血 (esophageal variceal hemorrhage). Its efficacy in coronary heart disease stems from its ability to dilate coronary arteries, lower blood lipids, and inhibit atherosclerosis. Additionally, in the context of liver cirrhosis-related complications, it helps reduce portal hypertension by decreasing portal and splenic vein diameters and improving blood flow dynamics, thus preventing variceal bleeding. Notably, it has received U.S. FDA Investigational New Drug (IND) approval, highlighting its recognized therapeutic potential [Data: Relationships (20564, 20566)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"丹参 is contraindicated in patients with bleeding tendencies\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Due to its well-documented 活血 (blood-activating) properties, 丹参 is contraindicated for individuals classified as 有出血倾向者 (those with a bleeding tendency), including those with coagulation disorders or excessive menstrual bleeding. This caution arises from the risk that 丹参 may exacerbate bleeding by interfering with normal hemostatic mechanisms. Clinical guidance explicitly advises against its use in such populations to avoid potential hemorrhagic complications [Data: Relationships (5427); Entities (14740)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"丹参 interacts with cytochrome P450 enzymes, posing drug interaction risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"丹参’s active components, particularly the lipophilic tanshinones, influence the expression and activity of CYP450 enzymes in the liver. This modulation can alter the metabolism of co-administered drugs that are substrates of these enzymes, potentially leading to clinically significant drug-drug interactions. While water-soluble constituents exhibit weaker effects, the overall impact of 丹参 formulations on CYP450 activity necessitates caution when used alongside other medications metabolized by this system [Data: Relationships (304)].\"\n        },\n        {\n      