ns by altering hepatic enzyme competition, further complicating hemostasis management. This interaction highlights a critical consideration for patients requiring hemostatic support [Data: Relationships (40183)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community presents moderate-to-high clinical impact due to the widespread use of 丹参-based therapies, significant drug interaction risks, contraindications in vulnerable populations, and implications for managing serious conditions like portal hypertension and fibrosis.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126571, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1399, "prompt_tokens": 6624, "total_tokens": 8023, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"丹参 and Related Therapeutic Entities\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on the herbal agent 丹参 (Salvia miltiorrhiza) and its derivative formulation 复方丹参滴丸, which are linked to multiple diseases, side effects, biological indicators, and patient populations through therapeutic indications, contraindications, and pharmacological interactions. Key relationships include丹参’s effects on vascular and liver-related biomarkers, its use in treating conditions like 食管静脉曲张破裂出血 and 口腔黏膜下纤维化, and contraindications for patients with bleeding tendencies. The community also includes related drug classes such as 止血药 and adverse reactions like 慢性肝病, 多囊卵巢综合征, and 血栓性疾病 associated with other medications.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"丹参 exerts multifaceted effects on vascular and fibrotic biomarkers\",\n   